WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:03.136
So 2022 was quite the year.

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:04.871 position:61%
Here's Bloomberg's two-minute round up.

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:05.672
In January,

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:06.706
the Federal Reserve laid

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:07.907
the groundwork to raise rates

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.476
to tackle the fastest inflation

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:10.543
in a generation.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.812 position:63%
Adding to global inflationary pressures:

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:14.547
Russia's invasion of Ukraine.

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:15.682
The attack began in late

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:17.584
February and dominated headlines

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:19.052
from the destruction on the ground

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:20.053
to US sanctions on

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:21.788
Russian banks and oligarchs.

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:22.922
By March, attention

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.190
zeroed in on the specific

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:25.825
threats that Russia posed:

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:27.894
restricting the flow of
natural gas to Europe

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:29.329
and attacks near a nuclear power

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:30.397
plant in Ukraine.

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:32.632
Corporate drama started
to pick up in April

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:35.068
when Elon Musk made a $43 billion

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:36.569
offer to take Twitter private.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:37.337
While Netflix

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:39.139
reported a loss in subscribers

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:40.407
and changed its strategy

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:41.875
to embrace advertising.

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:44.010
The theme in May: market mayhem,

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.745
as the Fed boosted the
size of its rate hike

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:46.980
to half a percentage point,

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.549
sending US stocks to 13-month lows.

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:51.151
While a single trader at Citigroup

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:51.851
made a mistake

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:53.253
that sparked a flash crash

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:54.687
in European stocks.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:57.057
Recession fears took root in June.

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:58.358
Half the headlines of Bloomberg's

00:00:58.358 --> 00:00:59.492
ten most-read stories

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:01.694
that month featured the R word.

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:02.762
Another R word:

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:04.164
Roe, after the Supreme Court

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:05.398
overturned Roe v Wade.

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:08.902
Geopolitics were the big

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:10.003
stories over the summer.

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:10.970
The killing of former

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:13.106
Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:14.908
and Nancy Pelosi defying China

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:16.209
when she visited Taiwan.

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:17.577
The UK lost its longest-

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:18.912
serving monarch in September.

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:20.180
Two weeks later,

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:21.014
the new Prime Minister

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:22.715
unveiled unfunded tax cuts

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:23.650
that caused the pound

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:24.517
to crash.

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:25.418
In October,

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.420
Credit Suisse became a meme stock

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.589 position:64%
setting new lows as some retail investors

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:31.758
bet the bank would go bust.

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:33.259
While Xi Jinping consolidated

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:34.994
his power, adding more loyalists

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:36.062
to China's leadership.

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:37.864
Crypto winter arrived in November

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:39.165
when FTX collapsed,

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:40.667
destabilizing the industry.

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:41.568
And by December,

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:42.836
bankers were tallying up

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:44.337
the cost from slumping markets

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:46.539 position:63%
sparked by the Fed's rate-hike campaign.

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:48.475
Their wallets will take
a hit as Wall Street

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:50.877 position:63%
firms prepare to slash year-end bonuses.

